id: 5
hanzi: 大象
pinyin: dà xiàng
level: HSK 5
part_of_speech: Noun

meanings_summary:
  en: elephant; large herbivorous pachyderm mammal
  es: elefante; gran mamífero paquidermo herbívoro de trompa prensil

senses[1]{sense_number,part_of_speech,register,definition_en,definition_es,example_phrase}:
  1 | Noun | Standard | a huge four-legged herbivorous mammal with a long flexible trunk, prominent tusks, and thick skin, native to Africa and Asia | mamífero terrestre de gran corpulencia, piel gruesa, grandes orejas y larga trompa móvil, propio de Asia y África | 一头大象 (an elephant)

example_sentences[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 在云南热带雨林保护区，一群野生大象悠闲地漫步在河边饮水嬉戏，引来无数观光客驻足。 | Zài Yúnnán rèdài yǔlín bǎohùqū, yì qún yěshēng dàxiàng yōuxián de mànbù zài hébiān yǐnshuǐ xīxì, yǐnlái wúshù guānguāngkè zhùzú. | In the Yunnan rainforest reserve, a herd of wild elephants leisurely ambled by the river drinking and splashing, drawing countless visitors to halt and watch. | En la reserva de la selva tropical de Yunnan, una manada de elefantes salvajes paseaba plácidamente junto al río bebiendo y retozando, atrayendo las miradas de los turistas.
  #2 | 大象具有高度发达的情感与群体记忆力，它们彼此照顾、尊重年长者的社交习性令人赞叹不已。 | Dàxiàng jùyǒu gāodù fādá de qínggǎn yǔ qúntǐ jìyìlì, tāmen bǐcǐ zhàogù, zūnzhòng niánzhǎngzhě de shèjiāo xíxìng lìng rén zàntàn bùyǐ. | Elephants possess highly developed emotional capacities and collective memories; their social habits of mutually caring and honoring matriarchs are truly marvelous. | Los elefantes poseen un extraordinario desarrollo emocional y una viva memoria colectiva; sus hábitos sociales de protegerse entre sí y acatar a los ancianos suscitan honda admiración.

